tuxdisplay (0.4.6) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Add an opt-in manager switch that keeps the host awake when its lid is
    closed while TuxDisplay is running.
  * Hold a logind sleep and lid-switch inhibitor for the exact lifetime of the
    display service and release it automatically on stop.
  * Report lid-close protection in status and diagnostics, and document power,
    battery, and ventilation implications.

 -- Tomas Pluharik <tpluharik@users.noreply.github.com>  Fri, 25 Sep 2026 12:20:00 +0200

tuxdisplay (0.4.5) unstable; urgency=critical

  * Stop treating OpenDisplay's decoder-starvation counter as proof of a failed
    USB session; it is expected to rise on damage-driven or low-FPS desktops.
  * Compare receiver FPS only when the sender queued enough frames to establish
    that the desktop was actively producing video.
  * Retain staged recovery for real packet loss and sustained active-stream
    underperformance, and log USB session boundaries for diagnosis.

 -- Tomas Pluharik <tpluharik@users.noreply.github.com>  Fri, 25 Sep 2026 12:00:00 +0200

tuxdisplay (0.4.4) unstable; urgency=critical

  * Accept the frame rate negotiated by Mutter and PipeWire instead of placing
    a conflicting fixed-rate constraint on the source stream.
  * Limit capture with a non-buffering pad probe so 15/30/60 FPS selection does
    not delay the first damage-driven frame.
  * Start and validate the video pipeline before opening the USB transport, and
    include the underlying GStreamer error when pipeline startup fails.

 -- Tomas Pluharik <tpluharik@users.noreply.github.com>  Fri, 25 Sep 2026 11:45:00 +0200

tuxdisplay (0.4.3) unstable; urgency=high

  * Keep Mutter, PipeWire, H.264, and OpenDisplay on one configurable frame
    cadence, defaulting to 30 FPS.
  * Gate every prediction chain on a fresh IDR and use receiver health reports
    to request recovery or reconnect a stalled cable session.
  * Validate OpenDisplay handshakes, try every attached Apple USB device, and
    keep the reconnect worker alive after unexpected protocol failures.
  * Stop the media pipeline before Mutter, bound every shutdown stage, and make
    GStreamer errors restart the user service.
  * Reauthenticate and reconnect the browser viewer after service restarts,
    release stuck browser input, and pause JPEG encoding while unused.
  * Reject stale tray state, expose receiver health in diagnostics, and monitor
    every critical process in the X11 compatibility workspace.

 -- Tomas Pluharik <tpluharik@users.noreply.github.com>  Fri, 25 Sep 2026 11:30:00 +0200

tuxdisplay (0.4.2) unstable; urgency=high

  * Fix a black OpenDisplay screen when the virtual monitor is initially static.
  * Pass PipeWire's first damage-driven frame directly to the encoders instead
    of holding it in a frame-rate filter until a second desktop update arrives.
  * Retain the initial browser frame and cache an H.264 keyframe so static
    desktops render immediately after a USB connection or reconnect.

 -- Tomas Pluharik <tpluharik@users.noreply.github.com>  Fri, 25 Sep 2026 10:20:00 +0200

tuxdisplay (0.4.1) unstable; urgency=critical

  * Prevent repeated OpenDisplay touch phases from aborting Mutter.
  * Translate slot-less OpenDisplay touch and Pencil input into guarded pointer
    button events instead of compositor touch slots.
  * Serialize USB input delivery on the GLib main loop and discard stale events
    after reconnects.

 -- Tomas Pluharik <tpluharik@users.noreply.github.com>  Fri, 25 Sep 2026 10:05:00 +0200

tuxdisplay (0.4.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Add native OpenDisplay protocol v3 streaming over usbmuxd.
  * Stream low-latency H.264 directly to the App Store receiver on TCP 9000.
  * Support USB operation without IP networking, Internet, or Personal Hotspot.
  * Forward OpenDisplay touch, scroll, and Pencil input into GNOME Wayland.
  * Keep the authenticated Safari/browser transport as a compatibility fallback.

